Package: roue
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: guilyx <guilyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-yaml, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.12), gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), ffmpeg, libvips-tools | imagemagick, libglib2.0-bin, libnotify-bin
Recommends: libvips-tools, libheif-plugin-libde265, libheif-plugin-aomenc, ghostscript, python3-nautilus, python3-xlib, pandoc
Suggests: libreoffice-writer, libreoffice-calc, libreoffice-impress, libheif-plugin-x265
Homepage: https://guilyx.github.io/roue/
Description: drag-and-drop file converter for the Linux desktop
 Roue converts files from a wheel of presets: HEIC to JPG, MOV to MP4,
 video to GIF, Word to PDF, "under 10 MB" for chat apps, and more.
 .
 Right-click files in Files (Nautilus) and pick "Convert with Roue…", press
 Super+Shift+D and drop files on the wheel, or use the roue command in
 scripts. Results land next to the originals and never overwrite anything.
 .
 The package also adds Roue's signed APT source, so Software Updater
 offers new versions.
 .
 Everything runs locally with FFmpeg, libvips, Ghostscript, Pandoc and
 LibreOffice. No uploads, no accounts, no telemetry.
